findings.body:
The previous implementation issued a single `repo.LoadMany(ids)` call; the new loop calls `repo.Load(id)` once per element, turning one round trip into N. For a repository backed by a database or a remote service this multiplies latency and connection pressure linearly with the size of `ids`, and the batch API is still available on `Repository`. The filtering (`Active`, `Owner.Enabled`) can be applied over the batch result instead:

```go
items := repo.LoadMany(ids)
results := make([]Item, 0, len(items))
for _, item := range items {
	if item.Active && item.Owner != nil && item.Owner.Enabled {
		results = append(results, item)
	}
}
return results
```

If `Load` also returns an error in the real interface, note that the loop as written discards any failure signal and would silently emit a zero-value `Item`.

